Tanks should position themselves against the back wall to avoid flying across the room.",Flags={F.Tank},Icon="INV_Misc_MonsterScales_14",Id="18500",Name="Wing Buffet"},{Effect="Onyxia breathes fire in a frontal cone, inflicting 3050 to 4000 fire damage to all enemies positioned in front of her.",Icon="Spell_Fire_Fire",Id="18435",Name="Flame Breath"},{Effect="Onyxia will cast Fear on everyone in intervals.\
\
Priests can use fear ward to help mitigate the fears on important members.",Flags={F.Important},Icon="spell_shadow_charm",Id="18431",Name="Bellowing Roar"},{Effect="Two Onyxian Hatcher appears after Onyxia lands back on the ground, assisting her for the rest of the fight.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Important},Id="onyxianhatcher",Name="Onyxian Hatcher",SubAbilities={{Effect="Onyxian Hatcher casts rains of fire that appears around the room, dealing heavy fire damage to any enemies inside.",Flags={F.Deadly,F.Important},Icon="spell_shadow_rainoffire",Id="rainoffire",Name="Rain of Fire"}}}}}},L="17966:100,18423:100,18705:40,18813:25,16900:11,16908:11,16914:11,16921:11,16929:11,16939:11,16947:11,16955:11,16963:11,30017:2,17064:8,17068:8,17075:8,17067:25,17078:25,18205:25"},
}}
ZLDB.R["TH"]={
Name="Timbermaw Hold",
Story="As ancient as Kalimdor itself, this enigmatic labyrinthine network of tunnels and caves beneath Mount Hyjal has been the home of the Furbolgs since well before the Sundering. Its halls are sacred among the tribes, a place of worship to their progenitors, the twin gods Ursoc and Ursol. Nowadays however, only wafts of putrid vapors escape the rotten caverns and whispers of venerating a foul god echo throughout Timbermaw Hold...",
Background=M.."raids\\th\\background",
GridBackground=M.."raids\\th\\grid-background",
MapId=44,
IconScale=0.8,
MinLevel=60,
MaxLevel=60,
Entrances={{MapContinentId=1,MapCoordinateX=16.8,MapCoordinateY=43.2,MapZoneId=30}},
Type=T.Raid,
Key="TH",
Bosses={
{Id="karrsh",Name="Karrsh the Sentinel",Story="A sentinel stands watch over something worth protecting. What Karrsh guards now in the dark of Timbermaw Hold, no one has returned to report.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\karrsh-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\karrsh-frame",MapCoordinateX=31,MapCoordinateY=73.5,L="33346:13,33345:13,33344:13,33343:13,33342:13,33341:13,33334:13,33333:13,33242:17,33241:17,33240:17,33239:17,33238:17,33237:17"},
{Id="rotgrowl",Name="Rotgrowl",Story="No title. No history. Only a name that the tunnels seem to have grown around, as if it were always there.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\rotgrowl-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\rotgrowl-frame",MapCoordinateX=15.1,MapCoordinateY=59.3,L="135:2,33346:13,33345:13,33344:13,33343:13,33342:13,33341:13,33334:13,33333:13,33248:17,33247:17,33246:17,33245:17,33244:17,33243:17"},
{Id="loktanag",Name="Loktanag the Vile",Story="The epithet was given by someone. Under what circumstances, and whether they lived to regret the proximity, is not recorded.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\loktanag-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\loktanag-frame",MapCoordinateX=14.7,MapCoordinateY=50,L="33249:13,33250:13,33251:13,33252:13,42290:2,42289:2,33256:13,33255:13,33254:13,33253:13"},
{Id="trioch",Name="Trioch the Devourer",Story="What Trioch has consumed, and what remains of it, are questions Timbermaw Hold has swallowed along with everything else.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\trioch-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\trioch-frame",MapCoordinateX=54.7,MapCoordinateY=64.7,L="42291:2,33293:13,33292:13,33291:13,33290:13,33289:13,33288:13,33287:13,33088:13"},
{Id="selenaxx",Name="Selenaxx Foulheart",Story="Whether the heart was always foul, or became so within these walls, the caverns do not distinguish between the two.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\selenaxx-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\selenaxx-frame",MapCoordinateX=45.7,MapCoordinateY=58.4,L="42190:2,42188:2,33286:13,33285:13,33284:13,33283:13,33282:13,33281:13,33280:13,33279:13"},
{Id="ormanos",Name="Ormanos the Cracked",Story="Something broke. The hold remembers neither what it was, nor what broke it - only that Ormanos remained after.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\ormanos-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\ormanos-frame",MapCoordinateX=32.4,MapCoordinateY=36.3,L="42292:2,42189:2,33263:13,33262:13,33261:13,33260:13,33259:13,33258:13,33257:13,33091:13"},
{Id="partath",Name="Chieftain Partath",Story="He leads what the hold has become. Whether he led it there, or merely inherited the ruin, is a distinction the tunnels do not make.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\partath-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\partath-frame",MapCoordinateX=22.2,MapCoordinateY=8.4,L="33271:13,33272:13,33273:13,33274:13,33275:13,33276:13,33277:13,33278:13,42287:2,42288:2"},
{Id="kronn",Name="Archdruid Kronn",Story="The title of Archdruid speaks to what Kronn once devoted himself to. The vapors drifting from Timbermaw Hold speak to what he devotes himself to now.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\kronn-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\kronn-frame",MapCoordinateX=42.4,MapCoordinateY=30.7,L="33084:13,33264:13,33265:13,33266:13,33267:13,33268:13,33269:13,33270:13,33333:13,33334:13,33341:13,33342:13,33343:13,33344:13,33345:13,33346:13,42187:2,42284:2,42285:2"},
{Id="ursol",Name="Ursol",Story="Ursol was a god of the wilds, twin to Ursoc, beloved among the furbolg since before the Sundering. He was many things. What he is now is something the old texts did not anticipate.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\ursol-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\ursol-frame",MapCoordinateX=49.5,MapCoordinateY=37.8,L="42177:100,33294:18,33295:18,33296:18,33297:18,33298:18,33300:18,33301:18,33302:18,33303:18,33304:18,33299:10,33305:10,58312:8"},
{Id="perotharn",Name="Peroth'arn",Story="He was a night elf, once. What he became afterward has many names, and what he is now has none that anyone has yet spoken aloud.",Portrait=M.."raids\\th\\perotharn-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\th\\perotharn-frame",MapCoordinateX=47.8,MapCoordinateY=30.5,L="42295:50,42307:50,33306:18,33307:18,33308:18,33310:18,33311:18,33313:18,33314:18,33315:18,33316:18,33317:18,33309:10,33312:10"},
}}
ZLDB.R["WORLD"]={
Name="Azeroth",
Story="The world of Azeroth is a realm scarred by eternal conflict and ancient magic. Beyond the confines of dungeons and fortresses, immense threats roam the open wilderness. Among these are the Dragons of Nightmare, once-noble lieutenants of the Green Dragonflight who have been driven mad by an insidious corruption. They now step through the portals of the Great Trees, intent on spreading their dark taint across the waking world. As the years went on, more and more threat emerged, making Azeroth an even more chaotic land.",
Background=M.."raids\\world\\background",
GridBackground=M.."raids\\world\\grid-background",
MapId=0,
IconScale=0.8,
MinLevel=60,
MaxLevel=60,
Type=T.Raid,
Key="WORLD",
Bosses={
{Id="6109",Name="Azuregos",Story="Azuregos is a powerful blue dragon who is trusted by Malygos with the safekeeping of the blue dragonflight's most precious artifacts.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\azuregos-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\azuregos-frame",MapCoordinateX=56.9,MapCoordinateY=86.1,MapId=1,MapZoneId=2,L="18704:100,17070:10,18202:10,18208:10,18541:10,18542:10,18545:10,18547:10,19130:10,19131:10,19132:10,83544:40"},
{Id="59963",Name="Cla'ckora",Story="Very little is recorded in the annals of Azeroth regarding Cla'ckora. Whether an ancient beast awakened from the deep or a forgotten monstrosity of a bygone era, its true nature and origins remain a complete enigma to even the most seasoned adventurers.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\clackora-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\clackora-frame",MapCoordinateX=69,MapCoordinateY=9.2,MapId=1,MapZoneId=2,L="55494:20,55495:20,55498:20,55501:20,55504:20,55496:17,55497:17,55499:17,55500:17,55502:17,55503:17,92020:5"},
{Id="92213",Name="Concavius",Story="Archivists and loremasters have found no definitive texts detailing the existence of Concavius. What dark forces summoned or birthed this entity is a mystery yet to be unraveled, leaving only terrifying rumors in its wake.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\concavius-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\concavius-frame",MapCoordinateX=82.1,MapCoordinateY=79.9,MapId=1,MapZoneId=7,L="83233:1,83234:1,83237:1,83238:1,83239:1,83240:1"},
{Id="80936",Name="Dark Reaver of Karazhan",Story="Though the horrors of Medivh's tower are infamous, this particular dark rider leaves no trace in the histories of Deadwind Pass. Who this reaver was in life, and what specific curse binds it to the mortal plane now, is a secret lost to the arcane madness of Karazhan.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\reaver-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\reaver-frame",MapCoordinateX=48.1,MapCoordinateY=75.8,MapId=2,MapZoneId=9,L="51769:1,51770:1,51771:1,51772:1,51773:1,51774:1,51775:1,51776:1,51777:1,51778:1,51779:1,51780:1,51781:1,51782:1,51783:1,51784:1,51785:1,51786:1,51787:1,51788:1,51789:1,51796:1,51797:1,51798:1,51799:1,51800:1"},
{Id="12397",Name="Lord Kazzak",Story="Kazzak is a battle-hardened doomlord and commander of Burning Legion forces. After the Third War, he remained on Azeroth in the Blasted Lands as Lord Kazzak.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\kazzak-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\kazzak-frame",MapCoordinateX=36,MapCoordinateY=75.1,MapId=2,MapZoneId=7,L="17112:20,18204:20,18543:20,18546:20,19133:20,17111:20,17113:20,18544:20,19134:20,19135:20,16045:1,83547:1,83545:40"},
{Id="91799",Name="Moo",Story="Moo. Moo moo moo, moo moo moo moo moo moo moo! Moo moo moo, moo, moo moo moo moo...",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\moo-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\moo-frame",MapCoordinateX=50.7,MapCoordinateY=54.7,MapId=39,Abilities={{Effect="Moo moos.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Deadly},Icon="Spell_Nature_Polymorph_Cow",Id="moomoo",Name="MOOOOOOOOO!"}},L="51261:100,60486:25,60487:50,60489:50,60490:50"},
{Id="16184",Name="Nerubian Overseer",Story="While the scourge of the fallen spider-kingdom is well documented by the Explorers' League, this specific overseer operates entirely in the shadows. Its distinct directives and exact place within the nerubian hierarchy are currently undocumented.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\overseer-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\overseer-frame",MapCoordinateX=9.6,MapCoordinateY=35.2,MapId=2,MapZoneId=12,L="83547:5,51730:1,51731:1,51732:1,51733:1,51734:1,51735:1,51736:1,51737:1,51738:1,51740:1,51739:100"},
{Id="80935",Name="Ostarius",Story="There are no surviving records in the great libraries of Dalaran or Ironforge that speak of Ostarius. The creature exists as a phantom in historical texts, with its motives and capabilities completely unknown to the scholars of the world.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\ostarius-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\ostarius-frame",MapCoordinateX=36.5,MapCoordinateY=80.7,MapId=1,MapZoneId=24,L="83480:1,83481:1,83482:1,83483:1,83484:1,83532:1,83485:1,83486:1,83487:1,83488:1,83530:1,83531:1"},
{Id="14889",Name="Emeriss",Story="Corrupted by the insidious Nightmare within the Emerald Dream, Emeriss has become a rotting, plague-ridden mockery of her former self. The dark magic sustaining her has given her the grim ability to spread disease and raise fungal rot from the corpses of her fallen foes.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\emeriss-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\emeriss-frame",MapCoordinateX=46.4,MapCoordinateY=36.1,MapId=2,MapZoneId=11,L="20644:100,20579:11,20580:11,20581:11,20582:11,20615:11,20616:11,20617:11,20618:11,20619:11,20599:14,20621:14,20622:14,20623:14,20624:14,65100:14,65101:14"},
{Id="14888",Name="Lethon",Story="Once a trusted lieutenant of Ysera, Lethon's mind was twisted by the Emerald Nightmare. His corrupted form is wreathed in dark magic, allowing him to drain the life essence from his enemies and unleash shadowy reflections of those who challenge him.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\lethon-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\lethon-frame",MapCoordinateX=62.3,MapCoordinateY=23.3,MapId=2,MapZoneId=33,L="20644:100,20625:14,20626:14,20627:14,20628:14,20629:14,20630:14,65102:14,20579:11,20580:11,20581:11,20582:11,20615:11,20616:11,20617:11,20618:11,20619:11"},
{Id="14890",Name="Taerar",Story="The madness of the Nightmare has fractured Taerar's very sanity and physical form. This tormented dragon of the Green Dragonflight now possesses the terrifying ability to summon phantoms and split his essence into multiple, deadly reflections of himself during battle.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\taerar-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\taerar-frame",MapCoordinateX=94.2,MapCoordinateY=35.7,MapId=1,MapZoneId=1,L="20644:100,20579:11,20580:11,20581:11,20582:11,20615:11,20616:11,20617:11,20618:11,20619:11,20577:17,20631:17,20632:17,20633:17,20634:17,65105:17"},
{Id="14887",Name="Ysondre",Story="Though Ysondre was once a benevolent guardian of the Emerald Dream, she has been driven to madness by the creeping Nightmare. She now roams the waking world, unleashing druidic magic twisted by corruption to strike down any mortals foolish enough to cross her path.",Portrait=M.."raids\\world\\ysondre-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\world\\ysondre-frame",MapCoordinateX=51.2,MapCoordinateY=10.9,MapId=1,MapZoneId=12,L="20644:100,20578:12,20635:12,20636:12,20637:12,20638:12,20639:12,65103:12,65104:12,20579:11,20580:11,20581:11,20582:11,20615:11,20616:11,20617:11,20618:11,20619:11"},
}}
ZLDB.R["ZG"]={
Name="Zul'Gurub",
Story="Hundreds of years ago, Zul'Gurub served as the capital city for the Gurubashi Troll Tribe, however, it was eventually destroyed by civil war and corruption from within. Centuries later, Atal'ai Priests have reclaimed the city for their own evil deeds, with the intention to summon their Blood God, Hakkar.",
Background=M.."raids\\zg\\background",
GridBackground=M.."raids\\zg\\grid-background",
MapId=12,
IconScale=0.8,
MinLevel=60,
MaxLevel=60,
Entrances={{MapContinentId=2,MapCoordinateX=52,MapCoordinateY=17.4,MapZoneId=29}},
Type=T.Raid,
Key="ZG",
Bosses={
{Id="14517",Name="High Priestess Jeklik",Story="High Priestess Jeklik is the Zandalari High Priestess of the Primal Jungle God Hir'eek, the Bat. Sent to Zul'Gurub to stop Hakkar the Soulflayer, she was eventually turned by the blood god.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\jeklik-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\jeklik-frame",MapCoordinateX=39.3,MapCoordinateY=73.3,Abilities={{Effect="Jeklik assumes the form of a bat until she is at 50% health.",Id="jeklikstage1",Name="Stage One: Bat Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Jeklik emits a piercing shriek, dealing 1,750 to 2,250 physical damage and silencing all enemies within a 30-yard radius for 10 seconds.",Flags={F.Magic,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Shadow_Teleport",Id="23918",Name="Sonic Burst"},{Effect="Jeklik charges towards an enemy between 8 and 40 yards away from her. The charge inflicts 1000 physical damage and silences its target for 5 seconds.",Flags={F.Magic},Icon="Ability_Warrior_Charge",Id="22911",Name="Charge"},{Effect="Jeklik summons a swarm of 6 to 8 bats, to help her throughout the battle.\
\
This occurs one minute into the fight and every minute after.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Nature_InsectSwarm",Id="5570",Name="Bat Swarm"}}},{Effect="Jeklik assumes her troll form when she reaches 50% health and alternates between her two spell casts.",Id="jeklikstage2",Name="Stage Two: Troll Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Jeklik begins casting a healing spell that restores 25% of her total health if not interrupted.",Flags={F.Interruptible,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Holy_Heal",Id="25807",Name="Great Heal"},{Effect="Jeklik channels a mind flay ability, dealing damage to a target and nearby allies if not interrupted.",Flags={F.Interruptible,F.Heal},Icon="Spell_Shadow_SiphonMana",Id="23953",Name="Mind Flay"},{Effect="Jeklik summons bat bombers that drop fire bombs on enemies, leaving burning patches on the ground that deal damage to anyone standing in them.",Icon="Ability_Hunter_Pet_Bat",Id="23974",Name="Summon Bat Bombers"}}}},L="19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19915:14,19918:14,19920:14,19923:14,19928:14,20262:14,20265:14,22711:10,22712:10,22713:10,22714:10,22715:10,22716:10,22718:10,22720:10,22721:10,22722:10"},
{Id="14507",Name="High Priest Venoxis",Story="High Priest Venoxis is the Zandalari High Priest of the Primal God Hethiss, the snake god. Sent to Zul'Gurub to stop Hakkar the Soulflayer, he was eventually turned by the blood god.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\venoxis-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\venoxis-frame",MapCoordinateX=51,MapCoordinateY=54.3,Abilities={{Effect="Venoxis assumes his troll form until he is at 50% health.",Id="venoxisstage1",Name="Stage One: Troll Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Venoxis's four snake adds will start the encounter with him, helping him during the fight.\
\
These adds should be killed before the beginning of stage two.",Flags={F.DPS},Icon="Spell_Nature_GuardianWard",Id="10713",Name="Venoxis' Snake Adds"},{Effect="Venoxis casts holy wrath, dealing 300 holy damage which increases for each enemy the spell bounces off of.",Flags={F.Heal},Icon="Spell_Shadow_SiphonMana",Id="23979",Name="Holy Wrath"},{Effect="Venoxis casts renew, healing himself for 2000 health every 3 seconds for 15 seconds.",Icon="Spell_Holy_Renew",Id="23895",Name="Renew"},{Effect="Venoxis creates an explosion of divine light, inflicting 875 to 1126 holy damage to nearby enemies.",Flags={F.Heal},Icon="Spell_Holy_HolyBolt",Id="23858",Name="Holy Nova"},{Effect="Venoxis cast holy fire, consuming an enemy in flames, dealing 2200 fire damage plus 125 fire damage every 2 seconds for 8 seconds.",Flags={F.Heal,F.Magic},Icon="Spell_Holy_SearingLight",Id="23860",Name="Holy Fire"}}},{Effect="Venoxis assumes the form of a snake when he reaches 50% health.\
\
Venoxis' damage is increased for the duration of the stage.",Id="venoxisstage2",Name="Stage Two: Snake Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Venoxis creates a poison cloud, dealing poison damage when stood in.",Flags={F.Poison,F.Deadly,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Nature_Regenerate",Id="12766",Name="Poison Cloud"},{Effect="Venoxis spits venom at an enemy, inflicting nature damage plus additional damage every 5 seconds for 10 seconds.",Flags={F.Poison},Icon="Spell_Nature_CorrosiveBreath",Id="6917",Name="Venom Spit"},{Effect="Venoxis spawns a parasitic serpent which attacks an enemy and poisoning them, dealing 300 nature damage every 2 seconds for 10 seconds.",Flags={F.DPS,F.Poison},Icon="INV_Misc_MonsterHead_03",Id="23865",Name="Parasitic Serpent"},{Effect="At 20% remaining health, Venoxis becomes enraged, increasing the damage he deals to his enemies significantly.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Enrage},Icon="Spell_Shadow_UnholyFrenzy",Id="3019",Name="Enrage"}}}},L="19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19900:17,19903:17,19904:17,19905:17,19906:17,19907:17,22711:10,22712:10,22713:10,22714:10,22715:10,22716:10,22718:10,22720:10,22721:10,22722:10"},
{Id="14510",Name="High Priestess Mar'li",Story="Mar'li is the high priestess of the spider loa, Shadra. Sent by King Rastakhan to Zul'Gurub to stop Hakkar the Soulflayer with the other loa high priests, she was eventually corrupted by the blood god.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\marli-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\marli-frame",MapCoordinateX=48.8,MapCoordinateY=78.8,Abilities={{Effect="Randomly throughout the fight, Mar'li will assume her spider form, gaining new abilities.",Flags={F.Important},Icon="INV_Misc_MonsterSpiderCarapace_01",Id="marlispider",Name="Spider Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Mar'li envelopes all enemies in a 10 yards radius with her webs, rooting them to the ground, increasing the time between their attacks by 100%, and preventing them from casting spells for 8 seconds.\
\
The off-tank needs to be ready to generate threat instantly as this will reset every rooted player's threat.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Deadly,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Nature_EarthBind",Id="24110",Name="Enveloping Webs"}}},{Effect="After assuming her spider form, Mar'li will eventually return to her orignal troll form, regaining her standard abilities.",Icon="inv_misc_head_troll_02",Id="marlitroll",Name="Troll Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Mar'li charges her target, dealing physical damage and stunning them.",Icon="ability_warrior_charge",Id="marlicharge",Name="Charge"},{Effect="Mar'li drains the life out of her target, draining 500 health every 1 second for 7 seconds.",Flags={F.Magic,F.Interruptible,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Shadow_LifeDrain02",Id="24300",Name="Drain Life"},{Effect="Mar'li hatches her eggs, birthing 4 Spawns of Mar'li that helps her throughout the fight.\
\
These spiders need to be dealt with as soon as possible as they will grow stronger as the fight goes on.",Flags={F.DPS},Icon="inv_egg_04",Id="marliadds",Name="Spawns of Mar'li"},{Effect="Mar'li shoots poison to all enemies in a 30 yards range, dealing 375 immediate nature damage and 290 periodic damage every 2 seconds for 10 seconds.",Flags={F.Poison},Icon="Spell_Nature_CorrosiveBreath",Id="24099",Name="Poison Bolt Volley"}}}},L="19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19871:17,19919:17,19925:17,19927:17,19930:17,20032:17,22711:10,22712:10,22713:10,22714:10,22715:10,22716:10,22718:10,22720:10,22721:10,22722:10,81003:10"},
{Id="11382",Name="Bloodlord Mandokir",Story="Bloodlord Mandokir is a powerful jungle troll and leader of the Gurubashi tribe. His constant companion is his raptor mount, Ohgan. He serves the evil god Hakkar the Soulflayer in Zul'Gurub along with the rest of his tribe.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\mandokir-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\mandokir-frame",MapCoordinateX=62.4,MapCoordinateY=69.6,Abilities={{Effect="Ohgan also becomes enraged when Mandakir is attacked, defending his master until death.",Icon="Ability_Mount_Raptor",Id="ohgan",Name="Ohgan",SubAbilities={{Effect="Ohgan sunders his target's armor, increasing the amount of damage they receive for every stack of Sunder Armor they are afflicted with.",Flags={F.Tank},Icon="ability_warrior_sunder",Id="ohgansunder",Name="Sunder Armor"}}},{Icon="INV_Misc_Head_Troll_01",Id="mandokir",Name="Mandokir",SubAbilities={{Effect="Mandokir gazes threateningly at a random enemy. If the targeted enemy casts any spell, Mandokir will charge them, inflicting heavy damage.",Flags={F.Deadly,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Shadow_Charm",Id="24314",Name="Threatening Gaze"},{Effect="Mandokir whirlwind into the enemies, dealing damage to every one of them in melee range.",Flags={F.Deadly},Icon="Ability_Whirlwind",Id="mandokirwhirlwind",Name="Whirlwind"},{Effect="Mandokir cleaves, dealing physical damage to all the enemies in front of him.",Icon="Ability_Warrior_Cleave",Id="mandokircleave",Name="Cleave"},{Effect="Mandokir charges at an enemy, dealing physical damage to them and stunning them for 2 seconds.",Icon="Ability_Warrior_Charge",Id="24408",Name="Charge"},{Effect="Every time three player gets resurrected by a Chained Spirit, Mandokir levels up, increasing the amount of damage he deals and reducing the amount of damage he receives.",Flags={F.Important},Icon="Spell_Holy_InnerFire",Id="mandokirlevelup",Name="Level Up"},{Effect="If Ohgan dies before Mandokir does, Mandokir becomes enraged for 1 minute, increasing the damage he deals to his enemies.",Flags={F.Deadly,F.Enrage},Icon="Ability_BullRush",Id="mandokirenrage",Name="Enrage"}}}},L="19872:2,22637:100,19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19863:8,19866:8,19867:8,19869:8,19870:8,19873:8,19874:8,19877:8,19878:8,19893:8,19895:8,20038:8"},
{Id="15082",Name="Edge of Madness",Story="Nearly nothing is known about the Edge of Madness, only the rumor that if you were to do an unknown invocation properly, one out of four possible legendary troll would be summoned...",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\edge-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\edge-frame",MapCoordinateX=59.8,MapCoordinateY=46.3,Abilities={{Icon="INV_Misc_Head_Troll_01",Id="grilek",Name="Gri'lek",SubAbilities={{Effect="Throughout the fight, Gri'lek will turn into an avatar, increasing his size and damage significantly but also reducing his speed. He will then start pursuing a random enemy regardless of threat.\
\
The targeted player must run away for the duration of the ability.",Flags={F.Deadly,F.Important},Icon="Ability_Creature_Cursed_05",Id="24646",Name="Avatar"},{Effect="Gri'lek creates ground tremors, stunning every enemies in a 20 yards radius for 2 seconds.",Icon="Spell_Nature_Earthquake",Id="6524",Name="Ground Tremor"},{Effect="Gri'lek roots an enemy, making them unable to move.",Flags={F.Magic},Icon="Spell_Nature_StrangleVines",Id="grilekroot",Name="Entangling Roots"}}},{Icon="Ability_Stealth",Id="renataki",Name="Renataki",SubAbilities={{Effect="Renataki vanishes, preventing enemies from being able to see him. Once he reappears, he will ambush a random enemy, dealing heavy damage.\
\
