{Id="14509",Name="High Priest Thekal",Story="High Priest Thekal is the Zandalari High Priest of Shirvallah, the tiger loa. Sent to Zul'Gurub to stop Hakkar the Soulflayer, he was eventually turned by the blood god.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\thekal-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\thekal-frame",MapCoordinateX=64.3,MapCoordinateY=34.7,Abilities={{Icon="Spell_Nature_Lightning",Id="lorkhan",Name="Zealot Lor'Khan",SubAbilities={{Effect="Lor'Khan casts a great heal on himself or an ally, healing them for 69375 health.",Flags={F.Interruptible,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Holy_Heal",Id="25807",Name="Great Heal"},{Effect="Lor'Khan surrounds himself with a lightning shield, returning some of the damage he takes back to the attacker.",Icon="Spell_Nature_LightningShield",Id="23552",Name="Lightning Shield"},{Effect="Lor'Khan disarms his target, forcing them to stop wielding their weapon for 6 seconds.",Icon="Ability_Warrior_Disarm",Id="22691",Name="Disarm"},{Effect="Lor'Khan and his allies are overtaken by bloodlust, increasing their attack speed by 75% for 30 seconds.",Icon="Spell_Nature_BloodLust",Id="24185",Name="Bloodlust"}}},{Icon="Ability_Stealth",Id="zath",Name="Zealot Zath",SubAbilities={{Effect="Zath does sweeping strikes, inflicting extra damage on another target for his next melee attack.",Icon="Ability_Rogue_SliceDice",Id="26654",Name="Sweeping Strikes"},{Effect="Zath gouges his target, incapacitating them.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Important},Icon="Ability_Gouge",Id="24698",Name="Gouge"},{Effect="Zath blinds his target, causing to wander around confused for up to 10 seconds.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Shadow_MindSteal",Id="21060",Name="Blind"},{Effect="Zath kicks his target, dealing physical damage and interrupting any spell currently being cast for 6 seconds.",Icon="Ability_Kick",Id="27613",Name="Kick"}}},{Effect="Thekal assumes his troll form for the duration of the stage up until him and all adds are dead at the same time.",Name="Stage One: Troll Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Thekal starts the fight with Zealot Lor'Khan, Zealot Zath and 2 Zulian tigers.\
\
Both zealots need to be tanked while the 2 tigers can easily be killed.\
\
Thekal, Lor'Khan, and Zath all need to die around the same time as they will otherwise resurrect each other.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Important},Icon="Ability_Mount_JungleTiger",Id="thekaladds",Name="Thekal's Adds"},{Effect="Thekal silences a random enemy, preventing them from casting any spells for 3 seconds.",Flags={F.Magic},Icon="Spell_Holy_Silence",Id="27559",Name="Silence"},{Effect="Thekal cleaves his current target, inflicting 150% weapon damage and leaving the target wounded, reducing the effectiveness of any healing by 50% for 5 seconds.",Flags={F.Tank,F.Important},Icon="ability_warrior_savageblow",Id="22859",Name="Mortal Cleave"}}},{Effect="Thekal gets resurrected ands assumes the form of a tiger for the duration of the stage up until his actual death.",Name="Stage Two: Tiger Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Thekal punches every enemies in a 45 yards radius, dealing 850 physical damage and knocking them back.\
\
Force punch also resets the threat. One of the tank that isn't currently tanking needs to be ready to pull aggro.",Flags={F.Tank},Icon="INV_Gauntlets_31",Id="24189",Name="Force Punch"},{Effect="Thekal summons 2 Zulian tigers, assisting him for the duration of the fight.\
\
Just like the Zulian tigers in stage one, these tigers can easily be killed and should be prioritized.",Icon="Ability_Mount_JungleTiger",Id="thekaltigers",Name="Summon Tigers"},{Effect="Thekal charges an enemy, dealing damage and stunning them.",Icon="Ability_Warrior_Charge",Id="thekalcharge",Name="Charge"},{Effect="Thekal goes into a frenzy, increasing his size and his attack speed by 50%.\
\
Hunters can use Tranquilizing Shot to remove frenzy from Thekal.",Icon="Ability_Druid_ChallangingRoar",Id="thekalfrenzy",Name="Frenzy"},{Effect="At 20% health remaining, Thekal becomes enraged, increasing the damage he deals to his enemies.",Flags={F.Enrage},Icon="Spell_Shadow_UnholyFrenzy",Id="thekalenrage",Name="Enrage"}}}},L="19902:2,19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19896:14,19897:14,19898:14,19899:14,19901:14,20260:14,20266:14,22711:10,22712:10,22713:10,22714:10,22715:10,22716:10,22718:10,22720:10,22721:10,22722:10"},
{Id="14515",Name="High Priestess Arlokk",Story="High Priestess Arlokk is the Zandalari High Priestess of the Primal God Bethekk, the panther goddess. Sent to Zul'Gurub to stop Hakkar the Soulflayer, she was eventually turned by the blood god.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\arlokk-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\arlokk-frame",MapCoordinateX=47.6,MapCoordinateY=20.8,Abilities={{Effect="Arlokk periodically summons stealthed panthers from the pens to attack players.\
\
While she is in troll form, off-tanks should control the panthers as damage dealers focuses on Arlokk.\
\
When Arlokk vanishes, players should shift priority to eliminating the active panthers.\
\
Upon her death, all remaining panthers will unstealth and attack the raid.",Flags={F.Tank},Icon="Ability_Mount_BlackPanther",Id="arlokkadds",Name="Stealthed Panthers"},{Effect="Arlokk assumes her troll form, which she begins the encounter in.\
\
She alternates between troll and panther forms throughout the fight, with transitions occurring more rapidly as the encounter progresses.",Flags={F.DPS},Icon="inv_misc_head_troll_02",Id="arlokktroll",Name="Troll Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="Arlokk gouges a target, inflicting 20 damage and stunning them for up to 4 sec.\
\
If the tank is gouged, the off-tank should taunt Arlokk. The main tank can taunt her back once they're back in control.",Flags={F.Tank},Icon="Ability_Gouge",Id="12540",Name="Gouge"}}},{Effect="Arlokk vanishes and assumes her panther form. \
\
She alternates between troll and panther forms throughout the fight, with transitions occurring more rapidly as the encounter progresses.",Icon="Ability_Mount_BlackPanther",Id="arlokkpanther",Name="Panther Form",SubAbilities={{Effect="While Arlokk is in stealth, she can mark a random player which causes every panther to focus on the marked target.",Flags={F.Heal},Icon="Ability_Hunter_SniperShot",Id="24210",Name="Mark of Arlokk"},{Effect="When Arlokk reappears in her Panther Form, she immediately casts Whirlwind, dealing heavy AoE damage to those nearby for two seconds.\
\
Melee should wait for the Whirlwind to fade before attacking Arlokk.",Flags={F.Deadly},Icon="Ability_Whirlwind",Id="24236",Name="Whirlwind"}}}},L="19914:18,19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19909:20,19910:20,19912:20,19913:20,19922:20,22711:10,22712:10,22713:10,22714:10,22715:10,22716:10,22718:10,22720:10,22721:10,22722:10"},
{Id="11380",Name="Jin'do the Hexxer",Story="Jin'do is a Gurubashi jungle troll witch doctor of considerable power. He is responsible for brainwashing the Zandalari priests Jeklik, Venoxis, Mar'li, Thekal, and Arlokk into the service of Hakkar, the Loa of Blood.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\jindo-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\jindo-frame",MapCoordinateX=31.6,MapCoordinateY=24.9,Abilities={{Effect="Jin'do curses a player, inflicting 175 damage every 2 seconds and spawns a Shade of Jin'do.\
\
Despite this, players are advised not to decurse this ability since only those afflicted by the curse can see and damage the Shades of Jin'do.",Flags={F.Curse},Icon="Spell_Shadow_UnholyFrenzy",Id="24306",Name="Delusions of Jin'do"},{Effect="Jin'do transforms the player with the highest threat into a frog.",Flags={F.Interruptible},Icon="Spell_Shaman_Hex",Id="24053",Name="Hex"},{Effect="Jin'do teleports a random player into the skeleton pit in the middle of the room.",Id="jindoteleportskeletonpit",Name="Teleport to Skeleton Pit"},{Effect="Jin'do curses players, spawning shades in his image, and summons wards that heal and brainwash throughout the battle to help him.\
\
Players should focus on killing all adds before attacking Jin'do.",Flags={F.Important},Id="jindoadds",Name="Jin'do's Adds",SubAbilities={{Effect="Though Shades of Jin'do are only visible to those cursed by Delusions of Jin'do, shades can attack anyone in the raid. They are also immune to AoE damage, and must be focused with single-target abilities and spells.\
\
Shades of Jin'do should be the first priority add to be killed.",Icon="race_troll",Id="14986",Name="Shade of Jin'do",SubAbilities={{Effect="Shade of Jin'do's melee attacks can interrupt spellcasts.",Icon="ability_meleedamage",Id="jindoshademelee",Name="Melee Attack"},{Effect="Shades of Jin'do casts dark magic that instantly lashes enemies, inflicting shadow damage.",Icon="Spell_Shadow_ShadowBolt",Id="24458",Name="Shadow Shock"}}},{Effect="Jin'do summons a powerful healing ward that heals Jin'do for more damage than the raid can deal.\
\
All players not actively killing a Shade of Jin'do should focus on this totem.\
\
Powerful Healing Ward should be the second priority add to be killed.",Flags={F.Heal,F.Important},Icon="INV_Relics_TotemofLife",Id="14987",Name="Powerful Healing Ward"},{Effect="Jin'do summons a brainwashing totem that mind controls players. The mind control cannot be dispelled without breaking this totem.\
\
Brain Wash Totem should be the third priority add to be killed.",Icon="INV_QirajIdol_Life",Id="15112",Name="Brain Wash Totem"},{Effect="When Jin'do teleports players into the skeleton pit, Sacrificed Trolls will spawn and attack the summoned person.\
\
Use AoE attacks to quickly free the summoned raid member.",Icon="INV_Misc_Bone_02",Id="14826",Name="Sacrificed Troll"}}}},L="22637:100,19716:11,19717:11,19718:11,19719:11,19720:11,19721:11,19722:11,19723:11,19724:11,19875:8,19884:8,19885:8,19886:8,19887:8,19888:8,19889:8,19890:8,19891:8,19892:8,19894:8,19929:8"},
{Id="14834",Name="Hakkar",Story="Hakkar the Soulflayer, the Blood God, is a malevolent and destructive loa notably worshipped by the Gurubashi trolls, and known in the troll pantheon as the Loa of Blood. He has taken control the Gurubashi Empire's fallen capital, Zul'Gurub.",Portrait=M.."raids\\zg\\hakkar-portrait",Frame=M.."raids\\zg\\hakkar-frame",MapCoordinateX=49.9,MapCoordinateY=39.8,Abilities={{Effect="Throughout the encounter, Sons of Hakkar spawn from the stairways leading into Hakkar’s chamber.\
\
When slain, they release a poison cloud that afflicts Poisonous Blood on any player who comes into contact with it.",Flags={F.Important},Icon="Ability_Hunter_Pet_WindSerpent",Id="11357",Name="Son of Hakkar",SubAbilities={{Effect="Poisons the player, dealing 100 damage every 3 seconds for 1.5 minutes.\
\
While afflicted, Blood Siphon will damage Hakkar instead of healing him.",Flags={F.Poison,F.Important},Icon="Spell_Nature_Regenerate",Id="24321",Name="Poisonous Blood"}}},{Effect="Hakkar stuns the entire raid and drains health from all players every second for 8 seconds, healing himself significantly.\
\
Players afflicted with Poisonous Blood instead cause Hakkar to take damage from this effect.\
\
To counter this ability, most of the raid must be poisoned before Blood Siphon begins.",Icon="Spell_Shadow_LifeDrain",Id="24322",Name="Blood Siphon"},{Effect="Hakkar can be engaged immediately upon entering the instance. However, if any High Priests remain alive, they empower him with additional abilities based on their aspects.",Flags={F.Deadly,F.Important},Id="hakkaraspects",Name="Aspects of the High Priests",SubAbilities={{Effect="Deals 1,300 to 1,700 damage to nearby enemies and silences them for 5 seconds.",Icon="Spell_Shadow_Teleport",Id="24687",Name="Aspect of Jeklik"},{Effect="Spits poison at nearby enemies, dealing Nature damage and additional damage every 2 seconds for 10 seconds.",Icon="Spell_Nature_CorrosiveBreath",Id="24688",Name="Aspect of Venoxis"},{Effect="Stuns the player with the highest threat for 6 seconds.",Icon="Ability_Smash",Id="24686",Name="Aspect of Mar'li"},{Effect="Increases Hakkar’s attack speed by 150%.",Icon="Ability_Druid_ChallangingRoar",Id="24689",Name="Aspect of Thekal"},{Effect="Gouges the player with the highest threat, stunning them for 2 seconds.",Icon="Ability_Vanish",Id="24690",Name="Aspect of Arlokk"}}},{Effect="Drives the player with the highest threat into a frenzy for 10 seconds, increasing their attack speed by 100% and movement speed by 150%, and causing them to attack nearby allies.",Icon="Spell_Shadow_ShadowWordDominate",Id="24327",Name="Cause Insanity"},{Effect="Approximately every 20 seconds, a player is afflicted with Corrupted Blood, taking 200 damage every 2 seconds for 10 seconds.\
\
This effect spreads to nearby players.",Icon="Spell_Shadow_CorpseExplode",Id="24328",Name="Corrupted Blood"},{Effect="After 10 minutes, Hakkar becomes enraged, greatly increasing his damage output.",Flags={F.Deadly,F.Enrage},Icon="Ability_Warrior_BattleShout",Id="hakkarenrage",Name="Enrage"}},L="19802:100,19852:14,19853:14,19856:14,19857:14,19864:14,20257:14,20264:14,19854:14,19855:14,19859:14,19861:14,19862:14,19865:14,19876:14"},
}}
